#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora.rst:54
#: 656106e76d8346d6a8243f5b7fd0039d
msgid "Upgrading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora.rst:57
#: bcf3c2f58a374a75976838ebde9a23f5
msgid "There are two ways to upgrade your template to a new Fedora release:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora.rst:59
#: 0ff29d1c7f024cc4ad66a199e6f9eb19
msgid ""
"**Recommended for most users:** :ref:`Install a fresh template <user/"
"templates/fedora/fedora:installing>`. After installing the new template, "
"install any new packages and redo any custom modifications you made in the "
"old template. :ref:`switch all qubes that were using the old template to the "
"new one <user/templates/templates:switching>`. You may want to note down "
"your customizations as you make them, and keep a note of any packages you "
"install. (You can also check the package logs in the old template using "
"``dnf history``.) This will help you recreate them in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora.rst:62
#: ef1f7676038f43a38002c26b64efe9c4
msgid ""
"**For advanced users**: :doc:`Upgrade the existing template in-place </user/"
"templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade>`. This preserves your current "
"customizations and installed packages without needing to redo them."
msgstr ""
